---
import Base from '@/layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHead from '@/components/PageHead.astro';
import { contactEmail, GITHUB_ISSUES, LEGAL_UPDATED } from '@/lib/contact';
import { adsenseClient, ga4Id } from '@/lib/ads';
const email = contactEmail(import.meta.env);
const adsOn = !!adsenseClient(import.meta.env);
const gaOn = !!ga4Id(import.meta.env);
---

<Base
  title="Privacy policy"
  description="What personal data AZ Studio (azsou.com) collects, why, where it is stored, which providers process it, and how you can access, export or delete it."
  crumbs={[
    { name: 'Home', path: '/en/' },
    { name: 'Privacy policy', path: '/en/privacy/' },
  ]}
>
  <PageHead eyebrow="Site & legal" title="Privacy policy" lede={`Last updated: ${LEGAL_UPDATED}`} />
  <div class="prose mt-8">
    <p>
      This policy explains how azsou.com (“AZ Studio”, “we”), a personal developer site run by Randy Hopkins,
      handles personal information when you browse, sign up, comment, write in the guestbook or subscribe. We
      collect as little as we can and store hashes instead of originals wherever possible. The Chinese version
      is at{' '}
      <a href="/privacy/" hreflang="zh-CN">
        /privacy/
      </a>
      ; both say the same thing.
    </p>

    <h2>Browsing</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Hosting logs</strong>: the site is hosted on Vercel, which logs technical data such as IP
        address, time and browser type for security and troubleshooting under Vercel’s privacy policy.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Local storage</strong>: your browser keeps your theme choice, sign-in session, a short-lived
        settings cache and an offline page cache. None of it is sent to third parties; see the{' '}
        <a href="/en/cookies/">cookie policy</a>.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Search</strong> runs in your browser (a static Pagefind index); queries are not sent to a
        server.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Videos</strong> show a locally hosted thumbnail; the YouTube player (youtube-nocookie.com)
        loads only after you press play, and Google’s privacy policy applies from then on.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Accounts, comments and the forum</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Sign-in (email and password, or GitHub / Google) is handled by Supabase Auth. Our database stores your
        email, display name, avatar URL and role; passwords are kept only as hashes by the auth service.
      </li>
      <li>
        Threads, replies, likes, bookmarks, reports and uploaded images are stored in Supabase (PostgreSQL and
        storage) behind row-level security. Forum posts and comments are public — please do not post sensitive
        personal details.
      </li>
      <li>
        Moderator actions are written to an audit log to prevent abuse. Exports and admin lists do not include
        emails.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Guestbook and link exchange</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        The guestbook stores only the nickname and message you type; entries are published after review.
      </li>
      <li>
        Link-exchange requests store the site name, URL, description and any contact detail you choose to give
        (admins only).
      </li>
      <li>
        For rate limiting we store a keyed client digest that cannot be turned back into an IP address. We do
        not store IPs.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Email subscription</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        We store your email, language and subscription status. Double opt-in: the confirmation link is valid
        for 48 hours.
      </li>
      <li>Confirmation and unsubscribe tokens are stored only as SHA-256 hashes.</li>
      <li>Every email has a one-click unsubscribe link.</li>
      <li>
        Mail is delivered by Resend or an SMTP provider configured by the site owner, only for delivery.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Bot protection (Cloudflare Turnstile)</h2>
    <p>
      Sign-up, guestbook and subscription forms use Cloudflare Turnstile, which reads technical browser
      signals to tell humans from bots under Cloudflare’s privacy policy. We only receive a one-time pass /
      fail token.
    </p>

    <h2>Analytics and advertising (Google)</h2>
    <p>
      {gaOn
        ? 'We use Google Analytics 4 to see which pages are read and where visitors come from. '
        : 'No third-party analytics is currently enabled; if we enable Google Analytics 4 it will work as described here. '}
      {adsOn
        ? 'We show ads through Google AdSense to pay for hosting and the domain.'
        : 'No ads are currently shown. If we start showing Google AdSense ads, they will work as described here and this date will change.'}
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Third-party vendors, including Google, use cookies (including the DoubleClick cookie) to serve ads
        based on your visits to this and other websites. You can opt out of personalised advertising in
        <a href="https://adssettings.google.com/" rel="noopener">
          Google Ads Settings
        </a>
        , or opt out of some third-party vendors’ cookies at{' '}
        <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/" rel="noopener">
          aboutads.info
        </a>
        .
      </li>
      <li>
        See{' '}
        <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" rel="noopener">
          how Google uses information from sites that use its services
        </a>
        .
      </li>
      <li>
        We implement Google Consent Mode v2: for visitors in the EEA, the UK and Switzerland, ad storage, ad
        user data, ad personalisation and analytics storage are all denied by default until you answer
        Google’s certified consent message (AdSense “Privacy &amp; messaging”, IAB TCF). Elsewhere you can
        turn ad and analytics cookies off at any time in
        <a href="/en/cookies/#choices">cookie settings</a>.
      </li>
      <li>No ads appear on admin, sign-in, form, subscription or legal pages.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Who processes data for us</h2>
    <p>We do not sell personal information. These providers process data only to run the site:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Vercel (hosting and CDN), Supabase (auth, database, image storage), Cloudflare (Turnstile).</li>
      <li>Resend or the owner’s SMTP provider (subscription email).</li>
      <li>
        Google (YouTube playback after you press play{gaOn && ', Google Analytics'}
        {adsOn && ', AdSense and consent management'}).
      </li>
      <li>GitHub (optional sign-in, and hosting of the site’s source code).</li>
    </ul>
    <p>These providers may process data outside your country.</p>

    <h2>Retention</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Account and posts: until you delete them or close your account.</li>
      <li>
        Unconfirmed subscriptions expire after 48 hours; unsubscribed addresses keep only the unsubscribed
        status.
      </li>
      <li>
        Rate-limit digests: only within the rate-limit window, then purged. Audit logs: kept to handle abuse
        and appeals.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Edit your display name and avatar in <a href="/settings/">account settings</a>; delete your own posts;
        unsubscribe.
      </li>
      <li>
        To close your account, delete all data or get a copy, contact us below; we act within 30 days after
        verifying it is you.
      </li>
      <li>
        Withdraw consent in <a href="/en/cookies/#choices">cookie settings</a> or by clearing site data.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Where local law (such as China’s PIPL, the GDPR or the CCPA) gives you more rights, we respect them.
    </p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>The site is for developers and creators and is not directed at children under 14.</p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <ul>
      {email && (
        <li>
          Email: <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>
        </li>
      )}
      <li>
        GitHub:{' '}
        <a href={GITHUB_ISSUES} rel="noopener">
          azsou/azsou-site issues
        </a>
      </li>
      <li>
        More options on the <a href="/en/contact/">contact page</a>.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      When this policy changes we update the date at the top. See also the{' '}
      <a href="/en/cookies/">cookie policy</a> and the
      <a href="/en/ad-disclosure/">advertising &amp; affiliate disclosure</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
